{"request_sha256": "bfbfcd6142181b84a8c8a9a6a1042ea247440f6f1004aab41e2864f6574107b3", "prompt_sha256": "847dd718e56258447ec5fcc89fdaadc9701165d02eab0b51001e616ebc1a0329", "dispatched_prompt_sha256": "f838010d2acd45b515a111b4560544542c98f381bef3acb0b180d9865bd3e984", "schema_sha256": "40b44f74e2832e0e52874cb964ff3f11b714cc6333ecca85f93378397c38d7cc", "model": "opus", "model_identity_basis": "claude CLI result event modelUsage key: claude-opus-5", "effort": "medium", "status": "ok", "forbidden_tools": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 4, "output_tokens": 11860}, "answer": {"passes": ["pass"], "defects": ["foliage.colour.mid-green-desaturated — render foliage reads brighter and more saturated, with yellow-green sunlit tips, against the reference's greyed, desaturated mid-green; secondary, non-defining, optional refinement", "crown.outline.irregular-asymmetric — render outline is a broad, near-symmetric dome; the reference's taller narrow leader section and one long outreaching limb toward the roofline are not reproduced; secondary", "habit.crown.pendulous-branchlets (character quality, not presence) — render strands are unusually uniform in length, spacing and near-vertical hang, reading as a regular fringe rather than the reference's varied, clumped curtains; presence is matched, so this is a refinement not a blocker", "bark.trunk.dark-rough-base (proportion) — dark basal section occupies roughly the lowest tenth of visible trunk in the render versus one-fifth to one-quarter in the reference; trait present, proportion short", "habit.trunk.single-leaning-stem (lean component) — render stem is essentially upright with only a slight sinuous curve and forks into two near-co-dominant limbs at low-mid height; the reference's pronounced left lean is absent. Single un-forked stem at ground level is matched, so the trait is supported; lean and fork height are reported as specimen variation, not a defining mismatch"], "observations": ["render-0 shows a single pale stem rising from a flat green ground plane, a darker grey-brown flared section over roughly the lowest tenth of the trunk, a low fork into two limbs, and a broad domed crown dominated by long near-vertical hanging shoots.", "Sky is visible through large parts of render-0's crown interior and between the hanging strands; foliage is carried as small discrete beads along the drooping shoots rather than as a solid mass.", "In render-0 primary limbs leave the stem at steep ascending angles and arch over into downward-pointing outer thirds at several heights.", "Crown apex in render-0 ends in thin sparse whip-like shoots against open sky with only scattered foliage.", "The lowest foliage curtain in render-0 stops roughly a third of tree height above ground, leaving a clear foliage-free trunk length beneath.", "Dark interior scaffold branches are visible through the gaps in render-0's crown, reading darker than the sunlit pale trunk.", "Thin, largely bare pale branches project from the crown at mid height on both left and right in render-0.", "reference-0 is a single ground-level S-WHOLE photograph in a garden setting; specimen relationship to the render is declared unknown, so no shared-individual or change-over-time claim is made.", "anchor-0 is used for finish/style only (its conifer morphology is irrelevant here); render-0's flat matte sky/ground plate and card-like foliage sit within the anchor's stylistic band.", "Leaf outlines, margins, catkins and trunk lenticel banding are not resolvable in either reference-0 or render-0 at the supplied scale."], "findings": [{"observation": "All six core traits (pendulous branchlets, open airy crown, pale upper trunk, dark rough base, single stem from ground, ascend-then-weep limb architecture) have directly visible support in render-0 matching the reference-0 statement.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Largest grounded gap: render-0's hanging shoots are highly regular — similar length, even spacing, near-identical vertical hang — whereas reference-0's curtains vary in length and clump unevenly along arching limbs.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Could follow from a uniform pendulous-shoot rule with little length or angle jitter, but no mechanism is observable from the images and none is required."}, {"observation": "Second gap: render-0's crown outline is a broad near-symmetric dome; reference-0 shows an irregular outline with a taller narrow leader at upper centre-left and a long limb reaching toward the roofline.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Third gap: foliage in render-0 is more saturated and yellower in the sunlit tips than the greyed mid-green of reference-0.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "render-0's stem is near-vertical and forks into two limbs at low-mid height; reference-0's stem leans markedly left with no fork over its visible length. Lean angle and fork height are individual-specimen attitude properties under an unknown specimen relationship, so this is recorded as acceptable variation rather than a defining mismatch.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Dark basal bark is present in render-0 but occupies a shorter fraction of trunk length than reference-0 describes; the blotchy, non-linear transition is present in both.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Catkins/reproductive structures and trunk lenticel banding cannot be assessed: unresolvable in reference-0 by the inventory's own account and not separable from foliage or bark shading in render-0.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Ground plane in render-0 is an untextured flat green surface with a cast shadow; reference-0 shows mown turf with a darker vegetated ring at the collar. Stem-to-ground contact and collar flare are legible in both, so the trait is supported; surface texture is a finish-floor matter within anchor-0's stylistic scope.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "anchor-0"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "No blocker identified: no core trait is contradicted by visible render evidence, and no core trait evidence is missing, clipped or ambiguous in render-0 (framing is complete).", "evidence_ids": ["render-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "habit.crown.pendulous-branchlets", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Long thin shoots hang near-vertically from arching laterals across the whole crown of render-0, forming continuous curtain strands from upper crown down to roughly mid-trunk and dominating the outer-crown silhouette, as reference-0 states. Uniformity of strand length and spacing is a refinement gap, not a failure of the trait."}, {"trait_id": "habit.crown.open-airy-texture", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Sky shows through large parts of the crown interior and between strands in render-0; foliage is carried as small discrete clusters along drooping shoots rather than a solid mass — matching reference-0's open, lacy reading."}, {"trait_id": "bark.trunk.pale-white-upper", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Main stem and larger ascending limbs in render-0 are whitish to light grey over mid and upper sections, contrasting clearly against the shaded crown interior, as in reference-0."}, {"trait_id": "bark.trunk.dark-rough-base", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "A distinctly darker, coarser grey-brown basal section with an irregular blotchy upper transition is visible at the foot of render-0's trunk. Present and correctly characterised; it spans a shorter fraction of trunk length than reference-0's one-fifth to one-quarter, recorded openly as a proportion gap."}, {"trait_id": "habit.trunk.single-leaning-stem", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "A single main stem rises from the ground plane in render-0 with no basal fork into co-dominant stems at ground level — the defining element of the reference statement. The pronounced lean is not reproduced (render stem is near-vertical) and a fork occurs at low-mid height; both are specimen-level attitude features under an unknown specimen relationship, reported as variation rather than silently dismissed."}, {"trait_id": "habit.branching.ascending-limbs-drooping-tips", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "render-0 repeats the ascend-then-weep architecture at several heights: limbs leave the stem at steep ascending angles, arch over and turn downward in their outer thirds with tips and shoots pointing groundward."}, {"trait_id": "foliage.leaf.small-fine-scale", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Foliage units in render-0 are very small relative to shoot length, reading as fine stippled points along hanging shoots. Leaf outline, margin and apex are unresolvable in both images, so only canopy grain is compared."}, {"trait_id": "foliage.colour.mid-green-desaturated", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "render-0's foliage is a brighter, more saturated green with markedly yellow-green sunlit tips, lacking the grey-tinged, lower-saturation cast of reference-0. Secondary priority and inventory-uncertain: a real mismatch, but not a blocker for reference character."}, {"trait_id": "crown.outline.irregular-asymmetric", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "render-0 presents a broad, largely symmetric dome without the taller narrow leader section or the single long outreaching limb described in reference-0. Secondary priority and non-defining, so it does not block the required cell."}, {"trait_id": "crown.top.slender-leading-shoots", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The apex of render-0 ends in thin whip-like projections against open sky carrying only scattered foliage, rather than a filled-out mass."}, {"trait_id": "branch.bare-pale-limb-left", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Thin, largely leafless pale branches project outward from the crown at roughly mid-height on both sides of render-0, including the left. The inventory marks this uncertain and it is a specimen-idiosyncratic feature; the render supports the general character."}, {"trait_id": "base.rootcollar.turf-contact", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The stem base in render-0 meets a continuous grassed ground surface with a modest collar widening and no basal cavity, mulch ring or paving. The untextured ground plane is a finish matter within anchor-0's stylistic scope."}, {"trait_id": "crown.interior.visible-dark-scaffold", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Dark interior scaffold branches form a visible network of crossing lines through the gaps in render-0's hanging shoots, reading darker than the sunlit pale trunk."}, {"trait_id": "canopy.lower-skirt-height", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The lowest foliage curtain in render-0 stops roughly a third of tree height above ground, leaving a clear foliage-free trunk length beneath, consistent with reference-0's skirt proportion."}, {"trait_id": "reproductive.catkins.unresolved", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Unassessable on both sides: reference-0 cannot separate catkins from foliage at its resolution, and render-0's shoot stippling likewise cannot be resolved into distinct reproductive structures. Unknown on evidence grounds, not treated as absent."}, {"trait_id": "bark.markings.lenticels-unresolved", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Horizontal lenticel banding, peeling papery strips and dark diamond fissures are not resolvable on reference-0's trunk; render-0 shows only broad tonal mottling and a few dark mid-trunk patches. No supported comparison is possible, so unknown."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-80-the-gap-loops-first-live-run","session_id":"df0c810b-4ed5-465b-943b-da844efed70d","tools":["StructuredOutput"],"mcp_servers":[],"model":"claude-opus-5","permissionMode":"default","slash_commands":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify","debug","code-review","simplify","batch","fewer-permission-prompts","doctor","loop","schedule","claude-api","workflow-authoring","run","run-skill-generator","advisor","agents","auto-mode-setup","autocompact","clear","color","compact","config","output-style","context","effort","fast","heapdump","init","mcp","import","model","__remote-workflow","workflow-launch-exec","reload-plugins","reload-skills","rename","ultrareview","security-review","usage-credits","extra-usage","usage","insights","recap","skill-doctor","goal","design-consent","design-revoke","list-agents","team-onboarding"],"terminal_slash_commands":["doctor","color","reload-plugins"],"apiKeySource":"none","claude_code_version":"2.1.278","output_style":"default","agents":["claude","Explore","general-purpose