s; foliage is carried as small discrete beads along the drooping shoots rather than as a solid mass.\", \"In render-0 primary limbs leave the stem at steep ascending angles and arch over into downward-pointing outer thirds at several heights.\", \"Crown apex in render-0 ends in thin sparse whip-like shoots against open sky with only scattered foliage.\", \"Lowest foliage curtain in render-0 stops roughly a third of tree height above ground, leaving a clear foliage-free trunk length beneath.\", \"Dark interior scaffold branches are visible through the gaps in render-0's crown, reading darker than the sunlit pale trunk.\", \"Thin, largely bare pale branches project from the crown at mid height on both left and right in render-0.\", \"reference-0 is a single ground-level S-WHOLE photograph in a garden setting; specimen relationship to the render is declared unknown, so no shared-individual or change-over-time claim is made.\", \"anchor-0 is used for finish/style only (conifer morphology is irrelevant here); render-0's flat matte sky/ground plate and card-like foliage sit within the anchor's stylistic band.\", \"Leaf outlines, margins, catkins and trunk lenticel banding are not resolvable in either reference-0 or render-0 at the supplied scale.\"], \"findings\": [{\"observation\": \"All six core traits (pendulous branchlets, open airy crown, pale upper trunk, dark rough base, single stem from ground, ascend-then-weep limb architecture) have directly visible support in render-0 matching the reference-0 statement.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"render-0\", \"reference-0\"], \"impact\": \"supported\", \"uncertain\": false, \"causal_hypothesis\": null}, {\"observation\": \"Largest grounded gap: render-0's hanging shoots are highly regular — similar length, even spacing, near-identical vertical hang — whereas reference-0's curtains vary in length and clump unevenly along arching limbs.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"render-0\", \"reference-0\"], \"impact\": \"optional\", \"uncertain\": fa